        "assignedTo": "Jenni Franano",
        "assignedToEmail": null,
        "dueAt": null,
        "completedAt": "2026-07-01",
        "comments": "The Scrub jay mitigation fee MUST BE PAID IN FULL PRIOR to ANY commencement of clearing activities on site. Not paying your mitigation fee and/or clearing during nesting season or clearing prior to making the full SJ payment will result in additional violation fees and a hold will be placed on your permit.If you choose not to utilize the county wide HCP you may request a review and determination from the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service.Per HCP guidelines, no woody vegetation removal is allowed during scrub-jay nesting season which runs from March 1 to June 30. It is the applicant’s responsibility to follow all mandated federal, state and county guidelines and regulations throughout the project. Failure to do so could subject you to enforcement action by the respective agency. Applicant must maintain a 25’ no disturb buffer from all potential gopher tortoise burrows.  If this is not possible, please contact the Florida Fish & Wildlife Conservation Commission for avoidance/mitigation measures prior to work starting or continuing.",
        "by": "Jenni Franano"
      },
